<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells record 373.3 trln lira 399-d bonds.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells record 373.3 trln lira 399-d bonds.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish Treasury sold a record 373.3 trillion lira of nominal-valued 399-day bonds in an auction on Tuesday at 112.42 percent yield, down sharply from 125.45 percent in the previous 392-day bond auction on December 24.</p>
<p>The previous record was 311.1 trillion lira of one-year bonds sold in an auction on October 25.</p>
<p>The central bank said bids for the auction totalled 469.4 trillion lira, down sharply from a record of 1,011 trillion lira in the October 25 auction.</p>
